WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:01.200
People love

00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:02.860
to hate Ayn Rand.

00:00:02.860 --> 00:00:05.180
You are out to destroy

00:00:05.180 --> 00:00:06.780
almost every edifice

00:00:06.780 --> 00:00:09.280
in the contemporary American way of life.

00:00:09.280 --> 00:00:10.360
60 years

00:00:10.360 --> 00:00:11.260
to the day

00:00:11.260 --> 00:00:13.292
after “Atlas Shrugged” was published,

00:00:13.300 --> 00:00:15.150
people STILL feel compelled

00:00:15.150 --> 00:00:16.360
to pan her.

00:00:16.360 --> 00:00:17.849
Ayn Rand became famous

00:00:17.849 --> 00:00:20.082
for her philosophy of objectivism

00:00:20.082 --> 00:00:22.010
which is a nice way of saying

00:00:22.010 --> 00:00:23.860
being a selfish asshole.

00:00:23.860 --> 00:00:26.100
Atlas Shrugged and Rand’s other books

00:00:26.100 --> 00:00:27.600
are about many such

00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:29.520
“self-interested people”.

00:00:29.520 --> 00:00:30.360
Mr. Rearden,

00:00:30.360 --> 00:00:32.980
you wouldn’t want it misunderstood that

00:00:32.980 --> 00:00:34.820
you work for nothing

00:00:34.820 --> 00:00:36.280
but your own profit?

00:00:36.280 --> 00:00:39.580
Indeed I want it understood clearly.

00:00:39.580 --> 00:00:42.920
And how does that benefit your fellow man?

00:00:42.920 --> 00:00:45.980
Thousands of jobs, billions in revenue,

00:00:45.980 --> 00:00:47.180
fueling our economy

00:00:47.180 --> 00:00:49.180
despite your efforts to destroy

00:00:49.180 --> 00:00:52.040
the very foundation of our existence.

00:00:52.040 --> 00:00:52.680
Rand argued

00:00:52.680 --> 00:00:55.720
that even if entrepreneurs and creators are “selfish”

00:00:55.720 --> 00:00:57.140
so what?

00:00:57.140 --> 00:00:59.780
They create opportunities for others.

00:00:59.780 --> 00:01:01.440
They never got that.

00:01:01.449 --> 00:01:03.390
But I’m glad these people do.

00:01:03.390 --> 00:01:05.290
They love Rand’s heroes.

00:01:05.290 --> 00:01:06.120
They had an idea,

00:01:06.120 --> 00:01:07.700
people told them “you can’t do that,

00:01:07.700 --> 00:01:08.840
that’s too selfish,

00:01:08.840 --> 00:01:09.680
that’s too

00:01:09.680 --> 00:01:10.940
out of the ordinary”,

00:01:10.940 --> 00:01:12.120
They did it anyways.

00:01:12.120 --> 00:01:13.540
And they’re successful.

00:01:13.540 --> 00:01:15.980
So being selfish themselves in the end

00:01:15.980 --> 00:01:17.540
helped out a lot of people.

00:01:17.540 --> 00:01:18.460
Through

00:01:18.460 --> 00:01:20.480
me wanting to make more money,

00:01:20.480 --> 00:01:22.100
I may create an invention

00:01:22.100 --> 00:01:24.980
that may improve the standard

00:01:24.980 --> 00:01:26.800
of living for millions and millions of people.

00:01:26.800 --> 00:01:27.640
These young people

00:01:27.640 --> 00:01:30.620
are part of an organization called “Turning Point USA”,

00:01:30.620 --> 00:01:32.580
a group that tries to get Atlas Shrugged

00:01:32.580 --> 00:01:34.540
read more on campuses.

00:01:34.540 --> 00:01:36.910
We’re on over 1100 college and high school campuses

00:01:36.910 --> 00:01:37.860
across the country.

00:01:37.860 --> 00:01:39.780
But the campuses are

00:01:39.780 --> 00:01:41.174
not listening to you

00:01:41.174 --> 00:01:42.720
or you’re a tiny

00:01:42.720 --> 00:01:44.820
fraction of the political discussion.

00:01:44.860 --> 00:01:47.120
You would be surprised at how big

00:01:47.120 --> 00:01:48.260
the following is

00:01:48.260 --> 00:01:50.460
and how much appetite there is actually for this.

00:01:50.580 --> 00:01:52.780
Atlas describes an America where government

00:01:52.780 --> 00:01:54.566
passes so many rules that

00:01:54.566 --> 00:01:57.160
most of the economy just shuts down.

00:01:57.160 --> 00:01:59.160
That idea horrified people who

00:01:59.160 --> 00:02:00.860
like regulation.

00:02:00.860 --> 00:02:02.090
I find it abhorrent.

00:02:02.090 --> 00:02:03.080
I really do.

00:02:03.140 --> 00:02:04.360
Why was the left so

00:02:04.360 --> 00:02:06.060
enraged by it?

00:02:06.070 --> 00:02:08.029
Because she was

00:02:08.029 --> 00:02:08.813
and is

00:02:08.813 --> 00:02:10.060
effective.

00:02:10.060 --> 00:02:12.200
She wasn’t talking about economics

00:02:12.200 --> 00:02:14.300
in terms of practical good.

00:02:14.300 --> 00:02:15.360
She was talking about

00:02:15.360 --> 00:02:17.680
your having a right

00:02:17.680 --> 00:02:19.060
to your own life.

00:02:19.080 --> 00:02:21.100
Jennifer Grossman of the Atlas Society

00:02:21.100 --> 00:02:22.840
loves seeing young people

00:02:22.840 --> 00:02:24.460
discover a new way to

00:02:24.460 --> 00:02:25.780
think about things.

00:02:25.780 --> 00:02:28.160
I’m a Peace Corps baby.

00:02:28.160 --> 00:02:30.185
I was raised in a community

00:02:30.185 --> 00:02:31.518
where I had never

00:02:31.518 --> 00:02:33.008
seen a conservative

00:02:33.008 --> 00:02:34.610
except in caricature.

00:02:34.610 --> 00:02:37.580
Libertarians were either stupid

00:02:37.580 --> 00:02:38.820
or evil.

00:02:38.860 --> 00:02:40.582
And when I went to Harvard,

00:02:40.582 --> 00:02:42.640
which was a bastion of liberalism,

00:02:42.640 --> 00:02:43.801
I actually found

00:02:43.801 --> 00:02:44.600
a couple of

00:02:44.600 --> 00:02:46.810
people who didn’t fit that stereotype.

00:02:46.810 --> 00:02:49.790
So I decided I needed to go back and do some thinking

00:02:49.790 --> 00:02:51.240
And some reading.

00:02:51.240 --> 00:02:53.760
She says she found the 12,000 page novel…

00:02:53.760 --> 00:02:56.700
a “spiritual experience”.

00:02:56.710 --> 00:02:57.710
Spiritual?

00:02:57.710 --> 00:02:59.730
It’s about business.

00:02:59.730 --> 00:03:02.730
I think it’s about overcoming odds.

00:03:02.730 --> 00:03:06.232
It’s about not allowing people to take advantage of you

00:03:06.240 --> 00:03:08.300
and feeling bad about pursuing your

00:03:08.300 --> 00:03:09.360
own interests.

00:03:09.360 --> 00:03:11.500
The consensus of the best metallurgical authorities

00:03:11.500 --> 00:03:12.960
are highly skeptical.

00:03:12.960 --> 00:03:17.700
I’m not interested in their opinions.

00:03:17.700 --> 00:03:18.760
Then whose do you go by?

00:03:18.760 --> 00:03:19.960
My own.

00:03:19.970 --> 00:03:22.589
In America, the social justice people are winning

00:03:22.589 --> 00:03:24.990
and people who wear dollar signs on their

00:03:24.990 --> 00:03:26.910
dress are vilified.

00:03:26.910 --> 00:03:29.460
They completely marginalized Ayn Rand.

00:03:29.460 --> 00:03:31.891
They completely took this stuff out of the classroom

00:03:31.900 --> 00:03:33.560
and now when they’re introduced to it,

00:03:33.560 --> 00:03:35.520
they freak out.

00:03:35.520 --> 00:03:37.360
In a good way, she means.

00:03:37.360 --> 00:03:38.280
People are surprised

00:03:38.280 --> 00:03:40.647
when they see how freedom-minded

00:03:40.647 --> 00:03:42.040
college students are.

00:03:42.040 --> 00:03:43.340
They’re socialists.

00:03:43.340 --> 00:03:44.400
They’re not socialists.

00:03:44.400 --> 00:03:46.710
Admittedly Bernie Sanders’ biggest portion

00:03:46.710 --> 00:03:48.800
of his support came from young people.

00:03:48.800 --> 00:03:52.040
But our generation is split in a really ironic way.

00:03:52.040 --> 00:03:54.505
60% think socialism is a good idea

00:03:54.505 --> 00:03:56.741
and then 70% say they don’t want to pay

00:03:56.741 --> 00:03:58.430
higher taxes and they don’t trust the government.

00:03:58.430 --> 00:04:01.020
So they just don’t understand what socialism really is.

00:04:01.020 --> 00:04:03.920
The first day of class we had a student that walked in

00:04:03.920 --> 00:04:05.880
and opened his laptop and on that

00:04:05.880 --> 00:04:08.520
laptop there were a ton of Bernie bro stickers,

00:04:08.520 --> 00:04:10.420
and “I love socialism”.

00:04:10.420 --> 00:04:12.080
So the very next day

00:04:12.080 --> 00:04:13.498
I brought to class a

00:04:13.500 --> 00:04:15.840
ton of stickers,

00:04:15.840 --> 00:04:17.000
laptop stickers that said

00:04:17.000 --> 00:04:19.960
“This laptop was brought to you by capitalism."

00:04:19.960 --> 00:04:21.180
Towards the end of the semester

00:04:21.180 --> 00:04:23.560
I had most of the class on my side.

00:04:23.560 --> 00:04:25.000
With the help of a book

00:04:25.000 --> 00:04:28.080
that’s 60 years old today.

00:04:28.090 --> 00:04:30.560
Fiction is more powerful than facts.

00:04:30.560 --> 00:04:32.000
Facts are more important,

00:04:32.000 --> 00:04:33.100
but maybe fiction

00:04:33.100 --> 00:04:34.680
does a better job teaching people

00:04:34.690 --> 00:04:35.990
what really matters.

